UID:event_316830574@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20261010T053022Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261020T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261020T203000
SUMMARY:Sapphic Book Club!  - September
DESCRIPTION:Queers to the Front!\nOur book club read for October is *Pumpk
 in Spice and Poltergeist* by Ali K. Mulford and K. Elle Morrison\n\n**Get 
 ready for a bewitching tale of love\, laughter\, and supernatural shenanig
 ans in the heart of Maple Hollow!**\n\nThe last thing apothecary witch\, J
 ordyn\, had on her mind was romance\, but when she got witchy-wasted\, she
  cracked open the coffin of her love life and conjured the ghost of her ex
 -girlfriend.\n\nJordyn is in for a spell of trouble now that the snarky sp
 ecter is determined to haunt her until she finds someone new.\n\nEnter Har
 low\, the new girl in town\, who just wants a job in her sister's cafe but
  she discovers that the spooky town of Maple Hollow is more than just a gi
 mmick. Real magic lives here. But after run-ins with vampires and one too 
 many grave cafe blunders\, she's ready to hop on a broomstick and fly out 
 of town. Until she finds herself falling under the spell of the enchanting
  witch who asks her on a date.\n\nAs sparks fly and cauldrons bubble\, wil
 l this unlikely pair brew up a love potion that defies the ghostly odds? O
 r will Jordyn's shade-y ex be the ultimate buzzkill to their budding roman
 ce?\n\nGrab your broomstick and buckle up for a cozy sapphic paranormal ro
 m-com that's sure to cast a spell on your heart this fall season!\n\n++\n\
 n[Read full synopsis here at The StoryGraph](https://app.thestorygraph.com
 /books/766aa577-f863-40ab-a07e-1f12f53d2a60)\n\n***\\*\\*\\****\n\nWe'll m
 eet at **White Duck Taco** in South Asheville \\(off Long Shoals Rd\\) \\|
 \\| Come early if you want some yummy food and drinks\\!
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/queers-to-the-front/events/316830574/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20261003T190043Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20261003T190043Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
