X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Meetup Haywood County Walking Meetup Group": "https://www.meetup.com/haywood-county-walking-meetup-group/events/316463898/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:meetup_haywood_county_walking_meetup_group
X-SOURCE:Haywood County Walking Group
UID:event_316463898@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20261010T053009Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261031T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261031T120000
SUMMARY:A Halloween Walk at the John C. Campbell Folk School in Brasstown 
 NC
DESCRIPTION:Haywood County Walking Meetup Group\nThe John C. Campbell Folk
  School is located in Brasstown\, Clay County\, NC. It has classes in over
  50 subjects\, including art\, craft\, dance\, music\, and nature. (My wif
 e took lap dulcimer lessons there many years ago. A family friend teaches 
 there regularly.) This is the place where John Jacob Niles first performed
  a song he had collected\, "I Wonder as I Wander".\n\nWe will gather in th
 e main parking lot of the campus. Our first stop will be at Keith House\, 
 where there are restrooms. We will go to the Craft Shop\, follow some trai
 ls\, visit the Herb Garden\, see the Eagle Dancer Sculpture\, and past a k
 iln. This is one walk where we will definitely not hesitate to stop and lo
 ok at various things there are to see. Your camera is a must on this one.\
 n\nOur route is 5 KM/3.1 miles. Tennis shoes are fine\, as there is no sig
 nificant elevation change. Most will not want walking sticks (although I p
 lan to take one). Bring a protein snack and plenty of water. Wheelchairs m
 ight have a somewhat hard time\, but trail strollers should be ok. If I re
 member\, dogs would probably be ok.\n\nBefore you leave\, you may want to 
 pick up lunch at the Folk School. You might bring a picnic lunch from home
 . Or you might catch some lunch after you have left campus and are on your
  way home.
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/haywood-county-walking-meetup-group/e
 vents/316463898/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260907T233950Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260907T233950Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Ncarboretum": "https://ncarboretum.org/event/guided-trail-walk-3/2026-10-31/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:ncarboretum
X-SOURCE:NC Arboretum
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261031T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261031T120000
DTSTAMP:20260710T074430Z
CREATED:20260710T074430Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260710T074430Z
UID:1778780019633-1793440800-1793448000@ncarboretum.org
SUMMARY:Guided Trail Walk
DESCRIPTION:Hit the trails and learn more about The North Carolina Arboretum’s botanically diverse forest with a guided trail walk! April through October\, this free hiking program is led by trained volunteer guides who take small groups of participants along woodland trails and through a variety of forest types. Depending on the season and each guide’s area of expertise\, topics of discussion may include wildflowers\, plant and tree identification\, natural history and more. \nGuided trail walks are limited to 15 people\, including the guide\, and are not recommended for guests under 16 years of age. Groups depart from the Baker Visitor Center Lobby on Tuesdays at 1 p.m. and Saturdays at 10 a.m. and 1 p.m.. \nWalks last 1.5 – 2.5 hours\, are approximately one to two miles in length. As this program is held rain or shine\, all participants should dress appropriately for the weather. \nThere is no pre-registration; walks are first-come first served and sign up sheets are located in the Baker Visitors Center. \nWalks are FREE; however\, donations to The North Carolina Arboretum Society are appreciated. Regular parking fees apply. Arboretum Society Members always park free. \nKnow Before You Go\n\nGuided Trail Walks are not recommended for guests under 16 years of age.\nGuided Trail Walks are rain or shine and all participants should be dressed comfortably and for the weather.\nHikes cover 1-2 miles and last 1.5-2 hours.\nWell-behaved leashed pets are welcome to accompany their owners. In the rare case that a pet is disruptive or negatively impacts the experience\, the pet and its owner may be asked to excuse themselves from the guided walk.
URL:https://ncarboretum.org/event/guided-trail-walk-3/2026-10-31/
CATEGORIES:Guided Trail Walk
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://ncarboretum.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/Birders-on-Cove-Hardwood-Trail-GSMNP-TN-Apr-16-1-1-1.jpg
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Ncarboretum": "https://ncarboretum.org/event/samhaim-a-creative-journey-through-this-threshold-of-autumn/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:ncarboretum
X-SOURCE:NC Arboretum
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261031T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261031T130000
DTSTAMP:20260924T183902Z
CREATED:20260924T141936Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260924T183902Z
UID:1778780019799-1793440800-1793451600@ncarboretum.org
SUMMARY:Samhain: A Creative Journey through Autumn’s Threshold
DESCRIPTION:Samhaim: A Creative Journey through this Threshold of Autumn\nwith Catherine Willows \nSaturday\, October 31  |  10 am – 1 pm \nRegister Here!\nSamhain marks a sacred threshold—the earth releases what is no longer needed\, and the Northern Hemisphere begins its descent into the darkness\, turning its energy inward toward the stillness of winter to come. We too are invited to slow down\, turning our attention toward the transitions and endings that have shaped our lives through this passing year. This is a season of mystery and the unknown\, time to discover what may be hidden beneath the surface: deeper knowing\, unexpected beauty\, new perspectives\, and possibilities that have yet to reveal themselves. \nTogether\, we will attune to Nature and this sacred season within the Arboretum gardens\, listen to the deeper rhythms moving through us\, and invite our intuition into the creative process. Through expressive artmaking\, we will enter this mid-autumn threshold and explore the mystery it holds. Artmaking becomes the portal through which we enter the mystery. Creativity becomes the elixir through which alchemy can open into discovery and transformation. \nNo artistic experience is needed\, only curiosity\, a willingness to listen inwardly\, and an openness to discover what reveals itself. If you have a journal\, bring that with you to use during the class but all other supplies will be provided. \nCatherine Willows is a Registered Nurse\, Certified Functional Medicine Health Coach\, and Transformational Creativity Coach\, and founder of Willows Coaching and Consulting. While holding sacred space\, she guides adults in awakening their inner creativity — moving beyond the demands of daily life into greater flow\, self-discovery\, and joy through intuitive art-making processes. Catherine believes creativity and our connection to the natural world are deeply interwoven — both vital pillars of wellbeing\, supporting nervous system regulation and inner equanimity\, and together essential for living a meaningful\, embodied life aligned with purpose and authentic expression. \n●  Members: Remember to enter your promo code upon checkout to receive your 10% member discount! Email adulteducation@ncarboretum.org with questions. \n●  See a full listing of Adult Education Programs at the North Carolina Arboretum here! Questions? Check our FAQs. \n●  We are committed to fostering a diverse\, supportive learning community. If the cost of a class is a barrier for you\, please complete this scholarship form and we will see what kind of assistance we can provide. \n●  Follow us on Facebook & Instagram! \n●  Join our Adult Education Student Hub on Discord! \n●  Interested in supporting the NC Arboretum more directly? Donate to the ONE Fund here. \nSee all of our classes open for registration here!
URL:https://ncarboretum.org/event/samhaim-a-creative-journey-through-this-threshold-of-autumn/
CATEGORIES:Adult Education
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://ncarboretum.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/pexels-borishamer-14516793.jpg
END:VEVENT
