UID:1013c4a7166de84f367add90dbecc20e@asheville.com
DESCRIPTION:Cost: 18.50-38.50 | Recurring on selected dates. On July 8\, 1
 944\, Private Booker T. Spicely boarded a bus in downtown Durham but never
  made it back to camp. The Black soldier\, newly stationed at a nearby Arm
 y base and unfamiliar with the South’s Jim Crow laws\, was shot twice in
