 ates between folk-rock\, alt-country\, and indie with a certain\, weather-
 worn intimacy. On her second album\, Vegas\, she turns bright lights and d
 ark waters into an exploration of quiet ruptures\, blurred memories\, and 
 grief\, guided by a voice that anchors even as it unfurls. w/ **lamplight 
 -** Songwriting project of Ian Hatcher-Williams // Folk that comes creek-s
 teeped
