BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Ncarboretum": "https://ncarboretum.org/event/sacred-forests-of-the-world/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:ncarboretum
X-SOURCE:NC Arboretum
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261107T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261107T150000
DTSTAMP:20261001T182539Z
CREATED:20261001T182539Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20261001T182539Z
UID:1778780020220-1794056400-1794063600@ncarboretum.org
SUMMARY:Sacred Forests of the World
DESCRIPTION:Sacred Forests of the World\nwith Alison Ormsby \nSaturday\, November 7  |  1 – 3 pm \nBRN – Elective \nRegister Here!\nThis class will explore the biological and cultural aspects of areas around the world that are conserved due to local beliefs and traditions.  Sacred natural sites include forests\, mountains\, and springs that have cultural significance.  Some sites also have taboos on use of species within the areas\, which serves a conservation function.  Most are not government-protected lands; rather\, are managed by local committees\, caretakers and/or religious leaders. Specific examples and research from India\, Ghana\, and Sierra Leone will be shared. Participants will discuss possible connections to forests in Western North Carolina. \nAlison Ormsby has a PhD in Environmental Studies and is a human ecologist with 30 years of experience working with people and protected areas\, environmental education\, and sacred natural sites. Alison publishes topics that relate to the interaction of people and nature\, including sustainable communities\, wildlife policy\, citizen science\, sustainable tourism\, and ethnobotany.  Her research focuses on conservation of sacred forests globally. \n●  Members: Remember to enter your promo code upon checkout to receive your 10% member discount! Email adulteducation@ncarboretum.org with questions. \n●  See a full listing of Adult Education Programs at the North Carolina Arboretum here! Questions? Check our FAQs. \n●  We are committed to fostering a diverse\, supportive learning community. If the cost of a class is a barrier for you\, please complete this scholarship form and we will see what kind of assistance we can provide. \n●  Follow us on Facebook & Instagram! \n●  Join our Adult Education Student Hub on Discord! \n●  Interested in supporting the NC Arboretum more directly? Donate to the ONE Fund here. \nSee all of our classes open for registration here!
URL:https://ncarboretum.org/event/sacred-forests-of-the-world/
CATEGORIES:Adult Education,BRN
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://ncarboretum.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Alison-bio-photo-India.jpg
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Ncarboretum": "https://ncarboretum.org/event/winter-buds-bark-tree-id-nov-26/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:ncarboretum
X-SOURCE:NC Arboretum
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261107T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261107T160000
DTSTAMP:20261001T183640Z
CREATED:20261001T183640Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20261001T183640Z
UID:1778780020221-1794056400-1794067200@ncarboretum.org
SUMMARY:Winter Buds & Bark Tree ID
DESCRIPTION:Winter Buds & Bark Tree ID\nwith Lauren Lampley \nSaturday\, November 7  |  1 – 4pm \nBRN – Core |  BREG – Elective \nRegister Here!\nEver wondered how you can identify a tree without its leaves? All tree species have different patterns of bark and leaf/flower buds that can be used to identify them even in winter time. In this program\, we will look closely at the common trees around the NC Arboretum trails and point out specific characteristics of their buds and bark so you can identify them even without their leaves. \nThis program will take place outside and will follow easy trails and paved walkways. Dress for the weather and prepare to be outside for the entire program time. \nLauren Lampley began her career at Grandfather Mountain Stewardship Foundation as a Park Naturalist which solidified Lauren’s interests in ecology and a passion for teaching others. She has led walks and hikes in a variety of subjects from Geology to Birding and especially enjoys learning and teaching about our local ecology. She currently works at the NC Arboretum as the Adult Education Coordinator managing all the programming hosted through the Adult Education Department. \n●  Members: Remember to enter your promo code upon checkout to receive your 10% member discount! Email adulteducation@ncarboretum.org with questions. \n●  See a full listing of Adult Education Programs at the North Carolina Arboretum here! Questions? Check our FAQs. \n●  We are committed to fostering a diverse\, supportive learning community. If the cost of a class is a barrier for you\, please complete this scholarship form and we will see what kind of assistance we can provide. \n●  Follow us on Facebook & Instagram! \n●  Join our Adult Education Student Hub on Discord! \n●  Interested in supporting the NC Arboretum more directly? Donate to the ONE Fund here. \nSee all of our classes open for registration here!
URL:https://ncarboretum.org/event/winter-buds-bark-tree-id-nov-26/
CATEGORIES:Adult Education,BREG,BRN
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://ncarboretum.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/PXL_20241216_171414529-2.jpg
END:VEVENT
